{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1107814-the-vaulderie","id":1107814,"title":"The Vaulderie","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-25T17:08:42-07:00","id":1107814,"title":"The Vaulderie","content":"Is the Vaulderie really as simple as mixing the blood of multiple kindred in a cup and drinking it? Is there sorcery or a discipline that has to supplement it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T20:37:02-07:00","id":1107868,"title":"","content":"There is actually some kind of rite involved, so I assume that knowledge of the Rite is essential for the vaulderie to work. I remember that Rituals was a background you could buy at character creation. And by being a background, it was something only the ST could award to characters afterwards - it couldn't be purchased by XP. Don't know how it is in V20 though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T07:18:53-07:00","id":1108018,"title":"","content":"The Vaulderie is a rite that has a supernatural element. V20 says, and I am paraphrasing, that simply putting the blood from a couple different vampires in a cup and drinking it is not sufficient for a Vaulderie.<br /> <br /> The subtext I've picked up is that the Vaulderie is an evil parody of the confection and consumption of the wine at a Mass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":2760,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","user":"Formosus","date":". 06-26-2017, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T14:02:37-07:00","id":1108138,"title":"","content":"The Vaulderie is starting to pass from cool to annoying. Trying to learn seems intentionally frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T01:28:23-07:00","id":1108318,"title":"","content":"It's a religious right that may or may not be powered by the Kupula or the faith of those involved. The entire right is about fanaticism as the trade off for losing the blood bond. Removing that diminishes the entire point of the Ritae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2763-nunboi","name":"nunboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2763_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T02:12:22-07:00","id":1108320,"title":"","content":"I believe it used to be that simple and you did it a few times like the Blood Bond. However, then the ritual was added to keep PCs from exploiting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T07:36:45-07:00","id":1108392,"title":"","content":"I don't think the ritual was added so much as to avoid any exploits, than as a way to explain why it took vampires thousands of years to figure out how to break the chains of their masters, when experimenting with mixing vitae would probably be one of the first things they would ever try to explore. Plus, it gives the Sabbat ritae some extra oomph.<br /> <br /> My take is that the ritual is only what breaks any existing bonds, and what makes the vinculum withstand subsequent attempts to bond someone who has taken part in it. Outside of that, I would have to think that, even without performing a ritual, drinking the mixed blood would still create the weaker bond between whoever participates, but who could then still be blood bonded to someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T07:39:32-07:00","id":1108399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1107814-the-vaulderie?p=1108138#post1108138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Vaulderie is starting to pass from cool to annoying. Trying to learn seems intentionally frustrating.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;We all dump our blood in a bucket and stir it&quot; is much worse than a religious rite in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11512-zanos","name":"Zanos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11512_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"550"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T07:51:26-07:00","id":1108403,"title":"","content":"I really fail to see the logic in just &quot;mixing our vitaes to try and break our bonds&quot;. Hence why it took them that long to figure out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T08:05:47-07:00","id":1108409,"title":"","content":"The Vaulderie along with most other ignobilis and auctoritas ritae contain a mystical element that requires some level of training, whether from a book or from a teacher. It doesn't necessitate that you know blood magic, but there's just enough debased koldunism in them to make them more than just mere pomp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T15:46:55-07:00","id":1108533,"title":"","content":"The Lore of the Tzimisce in Lore of the Clans is worth a read, specifically Kupala's Night.<br /> <br /> Basically there's a special relic of Kupala, the Sacred Fire Flower, which some powerful Proto-Sabbat Anarch Tzimisce stole from the Garou. They used its power to create an inferno which freed the spirits of those who jumped through it (the Flower's power is to bind and free spirits, and this can be used on the Blood Bond). With their bonds shattered, they began work on a rite which would borrow from the power of the Flower, and they ended up coming up with the Vaulderie, a communal blood bond which would displace the chains of the Elders and create a sense of camaraderie.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat wouldn't exist without Vaulderie, since it is a &quot;House of Contradictions&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T15:48:41-07:00","id":1108534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lordmagnusen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1107814-the-vaulderie?p=1108403#post1108403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really fail to see the logic in just &quot;mixing our vitaes to try and break our bonds&quot;. Hence why it took them that long to figure out.</div> </div> </div> </div>One blood bond displacing another at least makes a bit of sense. They're creatures of blood, and it is perfectly rational that something blood-related would free them from blood bonds. Remember that the Embrace (first death) frees you from blood bonds, so the idea of some kind of gift of blood freeing you from blood bonds isn't wholly novel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T17:31:02-07:00","id":1108561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zanos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1107814-the-vaulderie?p=1108399#post1108399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;We all dump our blood in a bucket and stir it&quot; is much worse than a religious rite in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the idea is that you create multiple blood bonds to other people to break it.<br /> <br /> Which means it's a STUPID way to break it.<br /> <br /> It's why shovelheads murder babies and kill old ladies on the orders of their sires because they're all brainwashed and crazy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T23:11:23-07:00","id":1108638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1107814-the-vaulderie?p=1108561#post1108561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the idea is that you create multiple blood bonds to other people to break it.<br /> <br /> Which means it's a STUPID way to break it.<br /> <br /> It's why shovelheads murder babies and kill old ladies on the orders of their sires because they're all brainwashed and crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, which is why the Anarchs split in two, the Sabbat became a murderous inhumane Death cult enslaved to their own community (and in short order, their Elders), and the Anarchs became powerless since they didn't have the Vaulderie and they didn't have organized totalitarian rule.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat and Camarilla aren't supposed to be good, they're both really shitty organizations with very different problems. Hunters Hunted ll gives a strong overview of them (paraphrasing): &quot;Oh, these ones sound nicer than the violent lot? Wrong. They're still monsters, they're just dairy farmers. We're their property, not their prey, and that's hardly a step in the right direction. I know some Hunters who have working relationships with the &quot;civilized&quot; Vampires and take out the worst of their kind though.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T00:18:07-07:00","id":1108651,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I always go with the idea the Sabbat are fundamentally a hypocritical organization. The Camarilla is controlled by their Elders but you at least have the reasonable freedom of action for most of your nights while the Sabbat have every single one of their actions dictated by their religious rites, their packs, and the fact their minds are bound to potentially hundreds of other Sabbat ranging from, &quot;I love this person enough to die for them&quot; to &quot;I just think Globitz the Flesh Skinner is the sweetest nicest guy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T06:38:10-07:00","id":1448850,"title":"","content":"How does The Vaulderie works exactly in terms of game mechanics in V20? Rulebook p289 states:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At times, a character may be at odds with herself over how to react to a given situation because of Vinculi she possesses toward another vampire. In cases such as these, the player should decide which party her character would favor outside the Vinculum. The character then rolls a number of dice for each party equal to her Vinculum score for that individual against a difficulty of 5 (for the party favored regardless of Vinculum) or 7 (for all other parties). The individual who receives the greatest number of successes earns the character\u2019s aid. Such is the nature of the Damned and the Vinculum \u2014 a character who knows better may sometimes be forced into an obviously bad course of action by following her emotions. </div> </div> </div>Lets say we have Bob and Alice. They share Vinculum towards each other with a rating of 5. Now lets say Bob steals money from Charlie and Alice is aware of that. Alice is a good person and she feels like she should turn him over.<br /> Here game mechanics kicks in. If we go by the book we have two options: turn Bob over or cover him up. Regardless of vinculum Alice would choose the first option. So the player rolls 5d10 with difficulty of 5 for first option and 5d10 with difficulty of 7 for the the second one. Alice choose the way which scores more succeses.<br /> Is that right interpretation of the rules? Because it feels like i'm doing something wrong.<br /> And I dont understand this statement at all:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Such is the nature of the Damned and the Vinculum \u2014 a character who knows better may sometimes be forced into an obviously bad course of action by following her emotions. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26785-alexey2040","name":"Alexey2040","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T18:10:17-07:00","id":1448919,"title":"","content":"It's saying that the emotional ties of the Vinculum can override a vampire's logic and judgement to make them act according to the blood-imposed loyalty even if it defies common sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T19:43:35-07:00","id":1448928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1107814-the-vaulderie?p=1448919#post1448919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's saying that the emotional ties of the Vinculum can override a vampire's logic and judgement to make them act according to the blood-imposed loyalty even if it defies common sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah ok, but do I understand rules correctly? I mean higher vinculum rating means more dice in dicepool. The more dice I roll, the higher the probabilyty that a roll with a difficulty of 5 would get more succeses than a roll with a difficulty of 7. In the example above, the higher Alices Vinculum rating, the higher the propbability that she would turn Bob over. Which is confusing because book states that the higher the vinculum the more loyal a person to that vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26785-alexey2040","name":"Alexey2040","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T19:52:35-07:00","id":1448929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alexey2040</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1107814-the-vaulderie?p=1448850#post1448850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does The Vaulderie works exactly in terms of game mechanics in V20? Rulebook p289 states:<br /> <br /> Lets say we have Bob and Alice. They share Vinculum towards each other with a rating of 5. Now lets say Bob steals money from Charlie and Alice is aware of that. Alice is a good person and she feels like she should turn him over.<br /> Here game mechanics kicks in. If we go by the book we have two options: turn Bob over or cover him up. Regardless of vinculum Alice would choose the first option. So the player rolls 5d10 with difficulty of 5 for first option and 5d10 with difficulty of 7 for the the second one. Alice choose the way which scores more succeses.<br /> Is that right interpretation of the rules? Because it feels like i'm doing something wrong.<br /> And I dont understand this statement at all:</div> </div> </div> </div>To my understanding here's how it would work<br /> Alice would feel pressured by the Vinculum to help Bob out by covering up for him. If she didn't want to do that, she'd need to make a roll to choose to do something else.<br /> <br /> Alice rolls 5d10 against a difficulty of 5 for her &quot;Help Bob, my Vinculum buddy&quot; roll. Then she rolls 5d10 against a difficulty of 7 for her, &quot;Choose to do smething else.&quot; If the first roll (DC 5) has more successes, then Alice feels pressured to help out Bob and would need to spend Willpower to try and resist helping Bob. If the second roll (DC 7) comes out higher, then Alice is free to choice whom to help. She could choose to rat Bob out of Charlie because she's pissed that Bob killed her ghoul last week, but Bob's still her friend and owes her, so when given the choice she still chooses to help him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-18-2021, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T21:38:11-07:00","id":1448937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1107814-the-vaulderie?p=1448929#post1448929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To my understanding here's how it would work<br /> Alice would feel pressured by the Vinculum to help Bob out by covering up for him. If she didn't want to do that, she'd need to make a roll to choose to do something else.<br /> <br /> Alice rolls 5d10 against a difficulty of 5 for her &quot;Help Bob, my Vinculum buddy&quot; roll. Then she rolls 5d10 against a difficulty of 7 for her, &quot;Choose to do smething else.&quot; If the first roll (DC 5) has more successes, then Alice feels pressured to help out Bob and would need to spend Willpower to try and resist helping Bob. If the second roll (DC 7) comes out higher, then Alice is free to choice whom to help. She could choose to rat Bob out of Charlie because she's pissed that Bob killed her ghoul last week, but Bob's still her friend and owes her, so when given the choice she still chooses to help him.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes much more sense to me. But contradicts with the rules as I understand them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The character then rolls a number of dice for each party equal to her Vinculum score for that individual against a difficulty of 5 (for the party favored regardless of Vinculum) or 7 (for all other parties) </div> </div> </div>&quot;for the party favored regardless of Vinculum&quot; - as I understand it meens the course of actions Alice feels right before any Vinculum mechanics or restrictions applies. Am I wrong? In the example above it is to turn Bob over to Charlie or police not to cover him up. Am I wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26785-alexey2040","name":"Alexey2040","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T22:57:01-07:00","id":1448940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alexey2040</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1107814-the-vaulderie?p=1448937#post1448937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It makes much more sense to me. But contradicts with the rules as I understand them.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;for the party favored regardless of Vinculum&amp;quot; - as I understand it meens the course of actions Alice feels right before any Vinculum mechanics or restrictions applies. Am I wrong? In the example above it is to turn Bob over to Charlie or police not to cover him up. Am I wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>A 'party' is a person or group of people. So forget what's right and wrong for a moment. Think about who Alice cares about the most between Bob and Charlie. If she likes Bob more, roll 5d10 with difficulty 5, and vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T02:36:42-07:00","id":1448955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alexey2040</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1107814-the-vaulderie?p=1448937#post1448937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It makes much more sense to me. But contradicts with the rules as I understand them.<br /> <br /> &quot;for the party favored regardless of Vinculum&quot; - as I understand it meens the course of actions Alice feels right before any Vinculum mechanics or restrictions applies. Am I wrong? In the example above it is to turn Bob over to Charlie or police not to cover him up. Am I wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I think I understand where you're misunderstanding. <br /> <br /> Out of character, Alice's player would decide whether Alice wants to help Charlie, or if Alice would rather help Bob. Then the player rolls Alice's Vinculumn rating at a difficulty of 5. This determines how many successes she gets to help the person she wants to help. Then she rolls her Vinculumn rating against a difficulty of 7. That is how many successes she garners towards helping the person she does NOT want to help.<br /> <br /> For example, Alice has a Vinculumn with Bob but personally detests him. Alice's player decides that Alice will help Charlie and will rat Bob out to him.<br /> <br /> So she rolls 5d10 against a difficulty of 5 and gets 4 successes to help Charlie, because he's the individual that Alice wants to help. Then the player rolles 5d10 against a difficulty of 7 and amazingly gets 6 successes. Alice wants to rat out Bob, but her Vinculumn tie causes her to instead back him up and cover for him.<br /> <br /> If she had rolled higher on the first roll, she would have been able to rat him out.<br /> <br /> Note that Vinculumn rolls are essentially extraneous if you want to help a pack mate and have no Vinculumn ties to the other target. If Alice's player decides Alice wants to help Bob and Alice has no tie to Charlie then it doesn't matter what the results of the rolls would be- she would help out Bob regardless of whether she got more successes on her roll to help Bob or roll to do something else.<br /> <br /> The Vinculumn roll is mainly there to make it harder to work directly against a packmate, but it's still entirely possible to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-19-2021, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T22:17:15-07:00","id":1449090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1107814-the-vaulderie?p=1448955#post1448955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I think I understand where you're misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> Out of character, Alice's player would decide whether Alice wants to help Charlie, or if Alice would rather help Bob. Then the player rolls Alice's Vinculumn rating at a difficulty of 5. This determines how many successes she gets to help the person she wants to help. Then she rolls her Vinculumn rating against a difficulty of 7. That is how many successes she garners towards helping the person she does NOT want to help.<br /> <br /> For example, Alice has a Vinculumn with Bob but personally detests him. Alice's player decides that Alice will help Charlie and will rat Bob out to him.<br /> <br /> So she rolls 5d10 against a difficulty of 5 and gets 4 successes to help Charlie, because he's the individual that Alice wants to help. Then the player rolles 5d10 against a difficulty of 7 and amazingly gets 6 successes. Alice wants to rat out Bob, but her Vinculumn tie causes her to instead back him up and cover for him.<br /> <br /> If she had rolled higher on the first roll, she would have been able to rat him out.<br /> <br /> Note that Vinculumn rolls are essentially extraneous if you want to help a pack mate and have no Vinculumn ties to the other target. If Alice's player decides Alice wants to help Bob and Alice has no tie to Charlie then it doesn't matter what the results of the rolls would be- she would help out Bob regardless of whether she got more successes on her roll to help Bob or roll to do something else.<br /> <br /> The Vinculumn roll is mainly there to make it harder to work directly against a packmate, but it's still entirely possible to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly how I understood it. The problem is the higher the vinculum rating the easier for player to ignore it. I mean in your example above the probability that 5d10(DC5) outscores 5d10(DC7) lower than probability that 10d10(DC5) outscores10d10(DC7). If Alice had higher vinculum rating towards Bob (let say it was 10) it would have been easier for Alices player to help Charlie rather then Bob. Which is kind of confusing and feels wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26785,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26785-alexey2040","user":"Alexey2040","date":". 05-21-2021, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26785-alexey2040","name":"Alexey2040","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}